            <ArticleTitle>[Argentine guidelines for the diagnosis, prevention and treatment of osteoporosis, 2015].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>46-60</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Osteoporosis is an evolving disease which affects over 200 million people worldwide. Our recommendations are guidelines for its diagnosis, prevention and treatment, but they do not constitute standards for clinical decisions in individual cases. The physician must adapt them to individual special situations, incorporating personal factors that transcend the limits of these guidelines and are dependent on the knowledge and art of the practice of Medicine. These guidelines should be reviewed and updated periodically as new, better and more effective diagnostic and therapeutic tools become available.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
